075 #edb/ref 17592186409830 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409833 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409831 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409833 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409833 1077 "selection" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409833 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409823 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409833 1079 #uuid "65142116-0d83-53ff-8a22-53c3c70d6112" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409834 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409824 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409834 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409825 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409834 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409826 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409834 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409829 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409834 1075 #edb/ref 17592186409832 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409834 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409834 1077 "selection" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409834 1078 #edb/ref 17592186409826 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409834 1079 #uuid "cd53fe12-9eba-5b4c-ab0e-a56e97b0b5d6" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409835 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409834 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409835 1069 "q-16098" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409835 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409835 1071 "The following table gives the values of functions $f(x)$ and ${f}^{′}(x)$ at some points. Find $({f}^{-1})^{′}(0).$\n\n| **$x$** | $f(x)$ | ${f}^{′}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| $2$ | $0$ | $-1$ |" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409835 1072 #uuid "14d699f1-906b-5c36-8ad3-387a50daa57f" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409835 1074 "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n({f}^{-1})^{′}(0)=\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${f}^{-1}(0)=2$ and ${f}^{′}(2)=-1.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(0) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(0))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-1)} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409836 1068 #edb/ref 17592186409833 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409836 1069 "q-15643" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409836 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409836 1071 "Consider the function $f(x)=12-6x$ and the point $P(3,-6)$ that lies on $y=f(x).$ Given that $f(x)$ is invertible in the vicinity of $P,$ determine the slope of $y={f}^{-1}(x)$ at the point $(-6,3).$" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409836 1072 #uuid "9c5ee55a-541c-5782-b80c-3f5d6eae3256" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409836 1074 "We start by calculating the derivative of $f$ at the point $(3,-6).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =12-6x \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-6 \\\\ {f}^{′}(3) & =-6\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(3,-6)$ lies on $y=f(x),$ we know that the corresponding point $(-6,3)$ lies on $y={f}^{-1}(x).$\n\nFurthermore, the slopes of the tangents to the two respective points are reciprocals. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}({f}^{-1})^{′}(-6) & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}({f}^{-1}(-6))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{f}^{′}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-6)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409837 1058 #edb/ref 17592186409838 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409837 1062 #uuid "176bf3b7-7f3b-537d-967f-47062e4a2221" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409837 1063 #edb/ref 17592186409835 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409838 1062 #uuid "a496245c-b30d-521d-bb6c-1805665cc858" 13194139533583 17592186045417 true] [17592186409838 1063 #edb/ref 17592186247113 